{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1133286-doppleganger-dilemmna","id":1133286,"title":"Doppleganger Dilemmna","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-23T22:16:01-07:00","id":1133286,"title":"Doppleganger Dilemmna","content":"Well, I've been helping a friend run a mostly-Vampire RP (with some Werewolf and Beast) on another site. All in all, things have been going well, if a bit slow because of everyone being busy, but recently I've run into a pretty big issue. One of our players plays a Daeva from the 1940's (I'll call her Beauty, for sake of simplicity) who was about to get married before a vampire (one of our planned villains) killed her groom and sired her. My character, made in conjunction with Beauty's player, was a Beast who for some reason looks and sounds exactly like the aforementioned groom.<br /> <br /> If you're thinking this sounds like an Inamorata, the vampire-weakening doppelgangers from <i>Thousand Years of Night</i>, then you're understanding the problem I have at the moment. I've started on this long before the book was released, but I had been planning on fleshing out why he was such a spitting image in case the GM friend needed potential plot ideas. I thought I had a lot of time to figure out this answer, though, but now that the GM, Beauty's player and I are all quite uncomfortable (we've already agreed not to have Inamorata be the answer for <i>numerous </i>reasons, including the fact that Beauty's player, a person who's had no problem getting really creepy in other games, was uncomfortable with going through with it), I need to figure out how what's really the deal with the Beast being such a doppelganger and fast. Does anyone have any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T23:25:48-07:00","id":1133290,"title":"","content":"The &quot;why&quot; doesn't matter so much as the &quot;how&quot;. It can remain a mystery, but if someone starts telling Beauty that if she pursues an affair with a long dead lost love that she'll go suicidal, see how that informs the drama.<br /> <br /> What was the original intent of having the beast reminisce the late groom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T00:56:17-07:00","id":1133298,"title":"","content":"If it's just a piece of the background. You could have it be a coincidence.<br /> <br /> I mean, people aren't great at remembering faces or voices and if the groom died in the 1940s, then at best the Daeva would have a few low quality photos to remember them. The Beast wouldn't have to be all that similiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T03:25:49-07:00","id":1133314,"title":"","content":"What is the exact timeline here and how complicated do you want it to be? How detailed is your Beast or the Groom's backstory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-24-2017, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T04:09:49-07:00","id":1133318,"title":"","content":"Is it possible the groom had a child out of wedlock and the Beast is his grandson? Or a brother (that he did or didn't know) and the Beast is <i>his</i> grandson?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T05:38:46-07:00","id":1133337,"title":"","content":"Or they simply 'look' a like - <b>many real world people do not really remember every possible detail of their loved ones</b>, just most striking things like 'dark brown hair', 'middle build', 'rosy cheeks'. After 70 years anyone exhibiting two of three those relative common similarities will 'look a like' for the elderly vampire to go on first conclusion 'he looks like my Groom!', even when, in reality, beside hair color - they are totally two different people. Memory is cheating us all whole are life!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/lkvOMt34hAo\" data-code=\"lkvOMt34hAo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lkvOMt34hAo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> To resolve this problem in game, let just Bride find good representation of his Groom visage - maybe colorful oil portrait. Not photos, as they do not survive long enough and photography in that time was not as detailed as painting. Then she will look on portrait of her Groom and be 'Wow, I really remembered him differently. This Beast is totally not him!' moment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If you run 2E game, you can even ad Condition for Bride vampiress to point that she - for now misleading Beast for the Groom, but then get Beats for sustaining relation for now, and then get's extra Beat for resolving the whole thing 'Ah, he totally is not my loved one!' scene. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}